From 98d00b84fc351144c7fde6a54cfb3787c0d800bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:16:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Pair tools: HV pad rule, hole keep-outs and DNP for
 TS06-DRV rev B

pcbkit: per-class pad rules (hard and soft) held by Board.check(), a copper
keep-out radius round the standoff holes (tracks and pads), KiCad rule areas,
the DNP attribute, a .kicad_dru writer with the IPC-2221B A6 rule text shared
with TS06-DISP (min 0.8mm, with units: KiCad ignores a bare number), and the
project's text floor. All opt-in: TS06-DISP regenerates byte for byte.

netroute: routes to the pad rules and to the hole keep-outs.

checkcopper: --hv-pad checks every HV pad against all other copper, pours
included (their fill when the file has it, else the zone clearance or the
.kicad_dru rule); footprints turned in KiCad's GUI are read with their
angle (red-team R11); roundrect pads are measured with their corner radius.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WoV3gyAFgmtuk6W6Dr4bdA
